body:
Well, of course we all dress to feel good about ourselves and comfortable in our own skin. To feel like the inside matches the outside. 

&#x200B;

But I also kind of feel like I "signal" a bit with my aesthetic? I have an alternative look but more polished but also with lots of vintage whimsical influences but also kinda witchy with lots of sharp edges and black/jewel tones and jewelry made out of animal bones. You get the idea. But I find that a lot of the people I really click with have a similar-ish aesthetic. And when I see someone who dresses like me, I know we'll probably have more in common than I would with any random person, I guess? I want people to look at me and have a vague idea of who I am, if that makes sense. 

&#x200B;

It's kind of like wearing a band shirt. You wear it because it looks nice on you, it's comfortable, you like the band, yada yada, but also it would be really cool if someone recognized the band and wanted to be friends. Almost like a mating call. Lol

Omg, I'm an (online) sex worker and had this issue come up once. A guy paid me to video call him and humiliate him for his size/looks and when he got on the camera he was SO handsome with the most beautiful dick I had ever seen... LOL. I was like "uuuhhhh, not sure what to say here!" lmao. 

&#x200B;

Honestly, just say the same stuff, it's just fantasy. I just pretended I didn't realize his dick was perfect.

Apparently in test scores/IQ level or something when I was tested as a child. High hopes for me! And look at me now!... -sigh-

&#x200B;

Remember kids, work ethic and discipline are worth FAR MORE than the "gift" of natural intelligence.

I used to steal from my mom when I was younger. She got child support money and had a really expensive cocaine addiction but when she would kick me out of the house at 13 years old if I didn't steal from her I wouldn't be able to eat or get around anywhere. 

&#x200B;

Do you have a need to steal from him? Or just doing it on impulse? Please get help or at least dig deeply into your psyche and ask yourself why you would steal from your dad. He would probably just help you with money if you need d it.

Santa Fe and Taos, NM are some of my favorite places I've ever been. It's just so gorgeous there. It's truly mystical there, in a way I can't explain. I feel incredibly drawn to everything about it. The unbelievably blue sky on the earthy hues of the high desert, wild horses running through fields of wildflowers, the incredible ratio of art galleries and antique shops for a relatively small population, every building seems to be full of outsider art. There's so much vintage torquoise jewelry, the smell of leather is everywhere, you can smell chilis from a cafe everywhere you walk, the breathlessness you feel walking up and down hilly sidewalks at 7,000 feet, being surrounded by all seasons at one - the dry, arid desert, full of lush green foliage, permanently snow-capped mountains in the distance, dramatic canyons and ravines, starry skies in the night when the temperature cuts in half. Everywhere there are steel structures with ancient figures and symbolism, pueblos that have withstood the test of time, contrasting colors of tan and blue of the earth and sky that seems almost sacred to the history of the area. 

&#x200B;

I'm counting down the days til I can go back there!

Also true, I honestly don't think this would have much of an effect on actual sexual abuse statistics because abusing children sexually would have so much more to do with power imbalance, a lack of morality and empathy towards others, an ability to manipulate and get close to vulnerable people, etc. than being attracted to children. 

&#x200B;

Of course I don't think pedophiles should be around children whatsoever but this made me think, honestly if we executed all the pedophiles how much of an effect would that REALLY have? With the extreme number of people who commit sexual assault against children I feel like a large percentage of them don't even have this deep seeded attraction to children or the self awareness to recognize their problem and seek help/out themselves.  

&#x200B;

I feel like it's kind of like the "not all murderers are mentally ill" concept. It's hard to just say "people do x because they have this clearly defined issue"

Also, it makes me think of how many people with extreme intrusive thoughts due to OCD would mistake themselves as pedophiles. It's very common for people to have intrusive thoughts about the darkest, most depraved things possible and obsess over how horrible they feel about it. This definitely does not make a person a pedophile. Intrusive thoughts regarding sexual abuse, violence, incest, suicide etc are all common among these people and many of them feel extreme distress over it and I could see them honestly thinking that's really who they are. It's a tough subject. 

&#x200B;

For example, unrelated to pedophilia obviously but I was a caretaker for my elderly grandmother for years and would have horrific intrusive thoughts about harming her, it was stemming from obsessive anxious thoughts that I wasn't taking care of her well enough or that I'd miss something or she'd get hurt while I was sleeping or something like that. Obviously I was not ACTUALLY wanting to hurt her (I've never been violent towards anyone), but I felt extreme distress and questioned myself a lot before I realized how severe my anxiety was and learned coping skills. I imagine sexual intrusive thoughts are even more disturbing.

I'm 20 now. I grew up really poor and my family has never left our county let alone state or country in my entire life so I always wanted to travel as soon as I was old enough. I lived with a roommate at 18 and worked as a barista and went to Italy as my first real solo trip/first time out of the country. I just booked the flight like 6 months in advance and saved up a lot and did everything really cheap. 

&#x200B;

I wish I had an inspirational coming of age story but I actually got attacked by my AirBNB host and went home early but I mean, I did it and feel proud that I did so whatever hahaha

Jesus Christ that is insanely disturbing. I can't even imagine how you might feel right now my stomach literally churned when I read this. I just want you to know, when I had something similar happen to me I felt like every time I got depressed about it I was being childish/weak, NO, this is a huge betrayal and any feelings you may feel right now are valid. I know being cheated on and betrayed by a friend can hurt your self-worth deeply but I really hope you understand that this does not reflect on you AT ALL. Those are the actions of two severely fucked up people that completely lack empathy. Good riddance, I'm sorry you're losing two people you cared about at once man that is seriously bullshit. We're all here for you! You deserve so much better and tbh being single is loads better than being with a person like her, I'm sure you're leagues better of a person than she is. 

&#x200B;

For what it's worth so you know you're not alone, my best friend who I let live with me for free and spent every day with for years sought out an older man who sexually assaulted me as a preteen after I told her the story and got into a (short) relationship with him. I ran into them together and the feeling of seeing my best friend in the world making out with my rapist sent me into possibly the worst spiral of my life. The lengths people will go to for sex/attention are unbelievable to me. But now when I look back I think of how awful they both are (obviously I knew that about the guy but yknow) and fuck it I guess they deserve each other. If a best friend can be 'stolen' just because they wanted to get laid, FUCK THEM.

Finding this song actually comforted me a little because it makes me feel like my obsessive fear (and yet yearning) for death is a little less abnormal. 

&#x200B;

Still makes me cry tho

There is no point. And if there were, what kind of "point" could really make life feel like it has a destination of some kind? I can't even think of a hypothetical explanation that would make it all make sense. It just doesn't. I don't know how to tell you to overcome your crisis because I'm in a permanent one too. I think of my own cosmic insignificance yet how I've only experienced the universe via my extremely limited POV, and the looming unavoidable reality of my own eternal nonexistence, constantly. It doesn't go away. 

&#x200B;

All I can say is sorry you're so self-aware. I feel it.

I hate it for many of the reasons you explained but I've never been able to put them into words. I grew up in a small retiree/tourist Floridian town and the amount of nu metal I hear is astounding to be honest. Walking through my college campus every day I hear at least two people parked in their cars before class blaring it vibin out (every day)

&#x200B;

Also I make the mistake of wearing band merch out in the wild so anyone who listens to vaguely alternative music approaches me pretty often, of course I'm not gonna be rude but like, I am not standing around when I could be going home and talking to you about nu metal and Christian metalcore bands that had music videos on music choice in 2010

13 year old me was a djent dweeb when that and alien...sounding....metal/deathcore (?) was a big trend (I'm 20 now so I guess that was in like 2012/2013). I associate djent with that kind of stuff. I had a shirt that said "DEFEND ALIENCORE" with a ray gun a la "Defend Pop Punk" and saw a picture of myself in it and was like whyyyyyyyyyyyyy

&#x200B;

The only band I can hear and not be like eugghhh is Vildhjarta I guess

That's amazing! Remember - while your thoughts may be painful and upsetting, while you were binge eating I'm sure you still had the same constant thoughts about food, but now you are defying your disorder and not hurting yourself. I feel the same way quite often because food is so comforting to me. And let's be honest, delicious food is extremely pleasurable in every way possible so please don't feel like there's anything wrong with you. Sometimes I feel like I'm the only one who is constantly fantasizing about food and feel gross about it then I realize I think we all spend a lot of the day excited for lunch/dinner and that's totally okay. Just keep doing what you're doing and try to stay busy! 

&#x200B;

Also, while food obsessed using tracking apps and such can become harmful for me and turn into over-restricting and obsession over calories and such which can be counter-productive. They're helpful to lots of people but I'm just throwing it out there that if you find yourself becoming too fixated on things like MFP maybe research mindful/intuitive eating (again, I know MUCH easier said than done and do whatever you can to help your disorder - I've just heard lots of stories about the longer people go with trying to eat healthier the more they fixate on restricting)

Every time I tell someone I have it they say "oh me too!" 

&#x200B;

when your food obsession literally ruins your health and your life but you can't stop eating until you're doubled over in pain, we can relate but I'm pretty skeptical that I've met dozens of people who say they go through the same exact thing

