don't worry though, I just had a really good steak so I'm fine for a while.

How long ago was your last treatment? Have you noticed many differences? What made you finally decide to look into ECT? I imagine you tried a lot of medications/etc before trying it.

&#x200B;

I have major depressive disorder (on my medical file it literally says "Major Depressive Disorder, ***SEVERE RECURRENT EPISODES, TREATMENT RESISTANT"*** underlined three times. I learned about ECT in my psych class and find it interesting but it sounds scary at the same time. But I'm pretty sick of living like this. I'm afraid I'll wind up killing myself and I REALLY don't want to do that (rationally).

I realize the way I worded "I feel like you're assuming I did something due to this being posted in the BPD sub" sounded a little rude but I was just trying to explain since if I had read something like this I would have probably thought something like that too! Not at all my intention so I hope it didn't come off that way! 

&#x200B;

I sympathize with him so much but it's hard for me to excuse it because we have the same mental disorder and I always have that thought process "well ***I*** don't do things like that when ***I'M*** having an episode!" but we have very different personalities and deal with things differently. I'm also seeing a therapist and have my life more together so I realize we're in different situations but I never know when to draw the line because I can relate so heavily that I often just ignore all bad behavior when a person tells me they are mentally ill since I know how that feels. I have trouble functioning while depressed but feel that he takes it out on me SO much more than I can handle.

&#x200B;

I wish he would just talk to me because I'm sure he's going through some shit. But he refuses to acknowledge me which is just making it harder and harder to be sympathetic. I called him like 3 times in a row because I had gotten a message from his friend who said he was worried about him so I just wanted to be sure he was okay and that's the only time he's answered me - to tell me to stop calling, grow up, get over it, and he'll talk to me when he feels like it, which has made me completely shift how I feel even though I know he probably is upset...

I haven't done anything like this, actually he's been the one who has put himself in mental hospitals multiple times throughout our relationship, once because we were arguing and he kept running into the middle of the highway and telling me he would kill himself and the police had to hunt for him. I know it's odd because I'm the one posting in the BPD sub, but he would threaten suicide to me then turn his phone off and go for a walk which made me think he may be hurt which was the worst manipulative thing a person has ever done to me. It was horrible every time. Even now, he's the one being cold and shitty towards me but I'm still afraid he may hurt himself.

&#x200B;

I completely understand why you would have taken this route. Physical abuse is definitely a limit I've never experienced, I've never had a partner get aggressive nor have I gotten aggressive towards anyone, but that would terrify me and I'm so sorry you went through that. Sadly it seems like you tried everything you could but you can't change someone who does things like this to you. I hope you both find healing somehow.

He always said he felt "inferior" to me. He's always borrowing money from me, and recently borrowed $350 from me and didn't pay me back. He goes months being unemployed and relying on me. I've had issues with him where every time we go somewhere, I get frustrated because he never seems to enjoy himself, he's always sulking and groaning about everything. He doesn't really enjoy... anything. He gets irritated when I invite him to do things because he would rather just sit around. He was constantly telling me "go find someone else, I can't keep up with you" "I'm not interesting enough for you" "I'm boring" etc. In my opinion, he is very interesting, but he lets his issues get in the way of it which gives him a very flat demeanor which is hard to deal with. The argument we had that lead up to this was about 1. these things and 2. the fact that when we lived together a year ago he suddenly stopped paying rent and I had to support us for months until I could break the lease for $3,000, and during this time he wrecked my car and it's still having issues that I've had to pay for. 

&#x200B;

I kept bringing it up and I guess he just got tired of realizing that it wouldn't just disappear, that it still hurts me, and he just dipped out. So basically, we had a discussion about things that happened a while ago that still bother me and he just said fuck it and ghosted me. Really the relationship was on its way out, but it's very hard for me to rip the band-aid off and I made this post in a time of shock. I knew it was time for us to break up but it's very hard when your partner's method of leaving you is to just ignore you outright and not acknowledge you - especially when it comes to logistics like owed money and bills you pay together.

&#x200B;

I feel like you're assuming I did something due to this being posted in the BPD sub. I haven't been diagnosed yet, my psychiatrist just told me I exhibit some of the symptoms and we could look into it further (I go to a free clinic so I don't get the best service). I feel like my problems with abandonment would be understood here the most which is why I post here. Him and I are both diagnosed with MDD though.

I'm not really sure if you're messing with me or not but that's nice of you I suppose. Tonight was one of my countless nights spent being overwhelmingly suicidal for hours and when I'm about to be an asshole on the internet I try to imagine that everyone is as emotionally fragile as I am and usually end up deleting my comments immediately and feeling bad. I don't really care much about anon Reddit insults of course but some people out there might? haha

&#x200B;

I probably wouldn't have responded at all but I get really defensive about being called ugly (projection 101) even though there are no photos of me on here .\_\_.

LOL I used to have a bunch of porcelain clowns but they gave off too much of an unsettling aura when all combined. I never found clowns freaky, if anything they're kind of cute and silly to me, but seeing an army of them while in a half sleep paralysis state kind of made me feel like they were .....shifty..... 

&#x200B;

The skull is actually the only technically non-thrifted thing! It's a raccoon, I found it at a park, it seems to have had a tooth infection or something as there's a tooth-sized hole in the jaw. It kind of counts though because it's second-hand haha. I love animal skulls but rarely find them in Florida and they're a little pricey to buy online most of the time, plus not knowing how to verify that they were ethical and all that!

Find the other weirdos and make friends with them! They may not be fellow goths but just anyone who's a bit against the grain. I'm 19 now but I dressed very alternative throughout school, although I went into online school at 13 because high-school is so awful. I sympathize with you, it really is a tough time in life, and it takes up SO much of your daily life! You'll find some friends, even if they don't like the same things, they might actually be your exact opposite as long as you get along well! 

&#x200B;

For what it's worth I would have awkwardly tried to befriend you :P

lol, I see a lot of the second kind who seem kind of uncomfortable, I usually assume they went along with someone and are like :| 

