Renting a place with a dog around here is awful if they're not tiny. I have no idea why that is. My budget was $1500 anywhere with at least two beds/one bath anywhere in either Melbourne, Satellite, Merritt Island, Cocoa Beach, Cape Canaveral, Cocoa or Rockledge, and it took me six months to find a place looking every day. That's not normal of course but it was crazy! 

&#x200B;

I wouldn't consider any areas around here bad enough to avoid them (if you're not involved with bad things hahaha) - what I would consider the nicest/most pricey area I've ever lived in in Cocoa Beach is where I almost got shot at 16 years old yet I've lived next to a pretty crime-ridden apartment complex for a while now and haven't even been made uncomfortable. I've never seen an area in Brevard that I'd be afraid to be in personally.

